# Path routing, so every route is a real URL the server is asked for. Netlify
# has no SPA fallback of its own; without this, /process/<id> is a 404 on a cold
# load and only works once the app is already running.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser must keep the URL it asked for so the router
# can read it. A genuine unknown path is answered by the app's own 404 page.
#
# Legacy URLs are not listed here — they are rewritten client-side in
# src/utils/legacyUrl.ts, which keeps one copy of the mapping and works for the
# Docker/nginx deployment too (docker/nginx/default.conf already has try_files).
/*  /index.html  200
